  "output": "On it — a sourdough feeding logger with time, ratio, and photo URL. Let me pull up the mini-app builder skill first.\n\nThis is a vibe build — no intake marker. Let me read the design doc and check existing state before scaffolding.\n\nTwo prior sourdough workspaces exist (`sourdough-feedings`, `sourdough-log`) — checking their state before I scaffold fresh.\n\nBoth are stale unpublished drafts from earlier sessions — I'll build fresh on the `sourdough-feedings` workspace. Checking what's already in it:\n\nA workspace already exists with a prior attempt. Let me read its source before rebuilding on it.\n\nThe prior attempt's source is solid and matches the skill's recipe. Let me check its CSS, then build.\n\nThe prior attempt is complete and doctrine-clean — it just never made it through QA/test/release. I'll make one small improvement (refresh the time field after logging so the next entry doesn't carry yesterday's timestamp), then run the full loop.\n\nBuild clean — 0 hard, 0 soft findings. Now QA across the viewport matrix:\n\nBuild staged but QA reports \"preview unavailable\" — checking the app state and retrying:\n\nQA still can't reach a preview. Waiting for the draft to propagate, then retrying:\n\nPersistent \"preview unavailable\". Let me inspect how `air-create qa` resolves the preview — the linked script may explain what's missing:\n\nQA mints a single-use preview token via `POST /api/create/preview-link`, then drives the browser. Let me see the raw API response for that call:\n\nThe API itself returns \"preview unavailable\". Calling it directly to see the full response:\n\nLet me get the error directly with curl through the same gateway path the script uses:\n\nThe control plane itself is returning HTTP 503 on the preview-link endpoint — the preview service, not the app, is the blocker. I'll retry a few times over a couple of minutes before giving up on this turn:\n\nPreview service is down hard (503 ×5 over two minutes). Let me confirm whether the dev release is gated the same way:\n\nBuilt and staged clean — zero findings — but I can't hand you a link yet: air's preview and release services are returning 503 right now (retried for several minutes; the QA pass and dev-link publish both route through them). The build itself succeeded and the draft is saved on the control plane.\n\nTap the card to peek at it from your phone, and when the service's back just say retry — I'll run the QA pass and publish the dev link.\n\n[card: app evalsuite-sourdough-feedings]",
